WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.919 --> 00:00:06.870
These days, it seems like everyone is making
money on the side.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:11.470
Your brother drives for Uber, your mother
rents out your old room on AirBnB, your sister

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:16.529
sells candles that smell like your grandma,
and your grandma is running a quilting blog.

00:00:16.529 --> 00:00:21.110
Almost 44 million Americans are reported as
having a “side hustle”.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:23.900
Most people start them for one of two reasons:

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.490
1:They want more income.

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:28.340
Or 2:
They want to start carving a path out of their

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.369
current job.

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:34.140
A side-hustle can definitely help you achieve
these goals, but not without proper research

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:35.340
and planning.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.739
So here are five things you need to know to
make sure that your side-hustle won’t be

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:41.540
hustling you.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:53.620
[MUSIC]

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:55.320
This is Jenny.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.839
Jenny wants to quit her job and work for herself
selling sweaters for hedgehogs.

00:00:58.839 --> 00:01:05.190
After all, she’s a member of the 20,000-strong
HEDGEHOGS FO LYFE Facebook group.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:09.780
If just 10% of those people bought a $30 sweater,
that’s $60,000!

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:15.130
That’s a nice dream, but before she starts
knitting, it’s time for a reality check.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:18.969
Are there people out there who are currently
making money at a venture like this?

00:01:18.969 --> 00:01:23.240
According to research done by Earnest Lending,
85% of side-gig workers make less than $500

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.479
a month.

00:01:24.479 --> 00:01:28.640
AirBnB has the highest average profit of $924
a month.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:34.179
Uber comes in 4th at $364 a month and Etsy
(where Jenny’s hedgehog sweaters will probably

00:01:34.179 --> 00:01:38.970
end up) is number 7 at a measly $151 a month.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:43.490
Maybe Jenny should sell a more established
product--like supplements or makeup--with

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:45.660
one of those network marketing companies.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:50.320
After all, she’s got facebook friends who are always
looking for new recruits.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:54.999
If you’re considering joining up with a
network marketing company, be extra cautious.

00:01:54.999 --> 00:02:00.399
According to a government study, only 1% of
network marketing participants actually turn

00:02:00.399 --> 00:02:01.509
a profit.

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:06.109
By law, these companies have to share some
of their financial data with you, like average

00:02:06.109 --> 00:02:07.109
income.

00:02:07.109 --> 00:02:11.260
Before diving into any new venture, you should
seek out every piece of information you can

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:15.140
get your hands on that will give you some idea
of how much you can realistically expect to

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:16.140
make.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:20.670
This is Tim.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:25.290
Tim found out that the going price of used
textbooks almost doubles around the beginning

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:26.300
of the school year.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:32.489
So, he figures if he sinks his savings of
$8,000 into a metric ton of Intro to Biology,

00:02:32.489 --> 00:02:36.400
he can sell them on Amazon in September and
double his money!

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.780
Not so fast, Tim.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:42.120
Just because you’re not making a product
doesn’t mean you won’t have COSTS.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.230
Tim will need somewhere to keep all those
books for the next 6 months, which means renting

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:51.340
a storage space; each book will have to be
mailed to the buyer, which means 400 individual

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:57.230
packing and shipping fees; and online retailers
like Amazon take a cut of every sale you make.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:01.860
Congratulations, Tim, you’re still making
a profit, but when you calculate how much

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:07.060
time you’re spending listing, selling, packaging,
driving from the storage space to the post

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:10.120
office… how much are you really making per
hour?

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:15.480
Essentially, Tim is the sole investor in his
own company, and no smart investor would put

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:20.930
a single dollar into a new venture without
seeing a honest list of expected costs and

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:21.930
revenues.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:25.409
If you want your side hustle to be a real
business, you’ve got to treat it like one.

00:03:25.409 --> 00:03:29.769
Which brings us to...

00:03:29.769 --> 00:03:33.659
Kendra wanted to make some extra money so
she started driving for Lyft on weekends.

00:03:33.659 --> 00:03:39.299
After 6 months, she had more cash in her pocket
and decided she liked it more than her day

00:03:39.299 --> 00:03:40.299
job.

00:03:40.299 --> 00:03:44.909
But since all the costs and earnings were mixed
up with her personal finances, she can’t

00:03:44.909 --> 00:03:47.629
tell whether it’s a good idea to go full-time.

00:03:47.629 --> 00:03:52.280
If Kendra had started a separate bank account
for her rideshare income, and paid for expenses

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:57.409
like gas, maintenance and car insurance strictly
from that account, she’d have a much clearer

00:03:57.409 --> 00:04:00.829
idea of how profitable her side-hustle really
is.

00:04:00.829 --> 00:04:02.799
You don’t need anything fancy.

00:04:02.799 --> 00:04:06.700
Just open a separate account in your individual
name at the place you’re currently banking.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:12.689
It’s a simple way to keep track of your
new income, and will make your life way easier

00:04:12.689 --> 00:04:14.209
come tax-time.

00:04:14.209 --> 00:04:19.190
Speaking of which….

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:24.160
After a year, Kendra’s made enough extra
money to put a down payment on a new car!

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.750
There’s just one problem.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:31.510
This is the most consistently nasty surprise
we see sneaking up on side-hustlers.

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:35.940
They’ve been making money from a new business
but haven’t put ANYTHING aside for when

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.540
the government comes knocking.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:41.370
We can’t stress it enough: Do not make this
painful mistake!

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:45.990
If it’s your first year as a side-hustler
and you don’t know how much you’ll have

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:51.620
to pay in taxes, start by setting aside 25%
of every dollar you earn for Uncle Sam.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:02.280
After your first year of business, you will
be required to pay an estimate of your taxes

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.970
on a quarterly basis.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:08.260
Just go to this website to set up an online
account directly with the IRS.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:13.560
Believe it or not, they actually make it pretty
easy to pay them.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:20.300
Jenny’s hedgehog sweater company is really
taking off thanks to an endorsement in Erinaceidae

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:21.310
Aficionado.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:25.690
But is it safe to quit her job at the widget
factory?

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:30.330
Before she leaps out of that plane, she needs
to make sure her parachute is big enough.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:35.030
First off: Does your side-hustle profit equal
at least half of what you make at your day

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:36.030
job?

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:40.810
If Jenny makes $3,300 a month at Widgets,
Inc. and her side-hustle is making a profit

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:45.630
of $2,000 a month, she’s probably in a safe
position to give her two weeks notice.

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:50.460
Second: Does she have 3 months worth of expenses
saved up for emergencies?

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:54.920
82% of small businesses fold because of cash
flow problems.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:59.910
If the market for hedgehog sweaters temporarily
dips, Jenny will need those funds to stay

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:02.020
afloat until it goes back up again.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:05.710
If that means she has to keep her day job
for a little while longer… well, that’s

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:08.600
better than having to ask for it back!

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:13.090
This might seem like a lot of work and planning
for something that was supposed to be “on

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:17.850
the side,” but it’s essential that before
you invest your time and money into a new

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:20.370
venture, you understand what you’re getting
into.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:25.180
It’s not uncommon for people, once they
find out what’s actually involved in starting

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:28.380
a side business, to decide they like their
day job more.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:32.520
That’s why your side hustle should be something
you genuinely like to do.

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:38.990
After all, extra money only has value if it’s
contributing to your overall happiness.

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:40.160
And that’s our two cents!

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:43.180
[MUSIC]

